WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.338
Hi! One English word can take several forms: success, succeed, successful, successfully. Today we'll learn how to pick the right form for a sentence.

2
00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:18.738
A noun names a person, thing or idea, like happiness or decision.

3
00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:23.034
A verb shows an action, like decide or succeed.

4
00:00:23.184 --> 00:00:27.138
An adjective describes a noun, like a dangerous road.

5
00:00:27.288 --> 00:00:32.658
An adverb describes a verb, like She ran quickly.

6
00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:43.002
Words in the same family have different forms. Success is a noun, succeed is a verb, successful is an adjective, and successfully is an adverb.

7
00:00:43.152 --> 00:00:50.274
Decision is a noun, decide is a verb, decisive is an adjective and decisively is an adverb.

8
00:00:50.424 --> 00:00:58.194
Danger is a noun, endanger is a verb, dangerous is an adjective and dangerously is an adverb.

9
00:00:58.344 --> 00:01:07.938
Endings give clues too. Nouns often end in -tion, -sion, -ness, -ment or -ity, like kindness and movement.

10
00:01:08.088 --> 00:01:15.330
Adjectives often end in -ful, -ous, -ive, -able or -less, like careful, famous and careless.

11
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.290
Adverbs often end in -ly, like carefully.

12
00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:26.634
Verbs sometimes end in -ify, -ise or -en, like beautify and widen.

13
00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:32.970
In a question, look at where the ___ is. The ___ of the plan: after the, we need a noun.

14
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:39.210
She smiled ___: it describes the verb smiled, so we need an adverb, like happily.

15
00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:46.866
It was a ___ trip: it comes before the noun trip, so we need an adjective, like wonderful.

16
00:01:47.016 --> 00:01:51.474
Watch out! She answered the question correct is wrong!

17
00:01:51.624 --> 00:01:58.386
It describes how she answered, so it describes the verb answered. We need the adverb correctly.

18
00:01:58.536 --> 00:02:05.154
Remember: adverbs describe verbs; adjectives describe nouns.

19
00:02:05.304 --> 00:02:16.170
Your turn! The firefighter was praised for his ___. Brave, bravery or bravely? Pause and think.

20
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:23.034
The answer is bravery, because after his we need a noun. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:23.184 --> 00:02:32.682
Another one! Please drive ___. Careful or carefully? Pause and think.

22
00:02:32.832 --> 00:02:41.178
The answer is carefully. It describes the verb drive, so we need an adverb. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:51.642
Last one! Forgetting the tickets was a ___ mistake. Care or careless? Pause and think.

24
00:02:51.792 --> 00:02:59.610
The answer is careless, because before the noun mistake we need an adjective. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:15.042
Remember: nouns, verbs, adjectives and adverbs are different forms in a word family. Check where the ___ is: after the comes a noun, before a noun comes an adjective, and an adverb describes a verb. Endings help too.

26
00:03:15.192 --> 00:03:19.770
Pick a word and try writing its whole family!

